# 3-Bus Power Flow Study

## Objective

A small power-systems study using PowerWorld Simulator to investigate how increasing electrical demand at Bus 2 affects the operation of a 3-bus transmission network.

## Software

- PowerWorld Simulator
- Microsoft Excel

## Method

A 3-bus power system was created in PowerWorld Simulator.

The power flow was solved using the Newton-Raphson method. The load at Bus 2 was then varied while monitoring:

- Bus 2 voltage
- Bus 3 voltage
- Generator output
- Total system losses

## Results

| Case | Bus 2 Load (MW) | Bus 2 Voltage (p.u.) | Bus 3 Voltage (p.u.) | Generator Output (MW) | Total Losses (MW) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Case 1 | 80 | 0.8991 | 0.8626 | 133 | 3.1 |
| Case 2 | 100 | 0.8925 | 0.8557 | 154 | 3.9 |
| Case 3 | 120 | 0.8852 | 0.8481 | 175 | 4.7 |

## Observations

Increasing the load at Bus 2 resulted in:

- Increased generator output
- Decreased voltage at Bus 2
- Decreased voltage at Bus 3
- Increased total system losses

This demonstrates how increasing demand can affect voltage levels, generation requirements and transmission losses within an AC power system.

